{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "lib": ["ES2021", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "outDir": "dist",
    "types": ["vitest/globals", "vite/client"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.vue", "tests/**/*.ts"],

  /* The page-render spec mounts the docs app, and importing its .vue files
     would drag them into this program — where they report the docs repo's own
     errors, chiefly that @exorgroup/apex-ui ships no declarations yet. That is
     the distribution work, deliberately left until last. The spec still runs
     under vitest, which does not typecheck; excluding it keeps this typecheck
     about the library. Revisit once dist/index.d.ts exists. */
  /* zz-hidden-reset reads the stylesheet with `fs`, because Vite stubs a CSS
     import to an empty string under vitest and the glob version of that guard
     silently compared against nothing. Node types are not installed here, so it
     is excluded for the same reason as the spec above. */
  /* service-stage mounts the docs app for the same reason, and drags in the
     same undeclared imports, so it is excluded on the same grounds. */
  /* zz-docs-classes reads the stylesheets with `fs` for the same reason
     zz-hidden-reset does — Vite stubs a CSS import to an empty string under
     vitest, which would make the guard pass by finding nothing. Excluded on
     the same grounds: Node types are not installed here. */
  /* zz-docs-vars reads the stylesheets, the components and the docs registry
     with `fs`, for the same reason again: it compares names across two repos,
     and an import would give it either a stubbed empty string or the docs
     repo's own errors. Excluded on the same grounds — Node types are not
     installed here, so `__dirname` reads as TS2304, which is a fatal class. */
  /* overlay-transition reads apex-ui.css to prove every overlay preset is
     quieted under prefers-reduced-motion. Excluded for the usual reason. */
  /* frozen-row-bg reads apex-ui.css to prove every row state publishes
     --apex-dt-row-bg for the frozen column to wear. Excluded for the usual
     reason: `fs` and `__dirname` with no Node types here. */
  /* switch-width reads apex-ui.css to prove a labelled switch still
     declares `align-self:start` — without it the switch stretches to the
     width of any help text beside it, which is how one rendered at 506px
     next to another at 84px. Excluded for the usual reason: `fs` and
     `__dirname` with no Node types here. `import.meta.url` is not a way
     round it — under vitest it is not a file URL and readFileSync refuses
     it. */
  /* button-size reads apex-ui.css with `fs` to prove the base rule READS the
     sizing variables its size rules SET — the two had drifted apart and every
     `size="sm"` button had been rendering at the md height since the component
     was written. An import cannot see it: Vite stubs a CSS import to an empty
     string under vitest. Excluded on the same grounds as the rest — no Node
     types here, so `__dirname` reads as TS2304, which IS a fatal class, and
     this guard caught itself. */
  /* editor-engine reads node_modules to prove the ten prosemirror packages
     resolved to one copy each. The Vite-glob form of that check was written
     first precisely to avoid this exclusion, and it was inert: import.meta.glob
     does not descend into node_modules, so it matched nothing and passed with a
     duplicate planted. Excluded on the same grounds as the rest. */
  /* form-modal-width reads apex-ui.css to prove the modal panel's width is a
     variable a host can set rather than a literal. Excluded for the usual
     reason: `fs` and `__dirname` with no Node types here. */
  "exclude": [
    "tests/form-modal-width.spec.ts",
    "tests/button-size.spec.ts",
    "tests/overlay-transition.spec.ts",
    "tests/frozen-row-bg.spec.ts",
    "tests/editor-engine.spec.ts",
    "tests/zz-docs-pages.spec.ts",
    "tests/zz-docs-classes.spec.ts",
    "tests/zz-docs-vars.spec.ts",
    "tests/zz-var-families.spec.ts",
    "tests/zz-hidden-reset.spec.ts",
    "tests/service-stage.spec.ts",
    "tests/alert-ui.spec.ts",
    "tests/switch-width.spec.ts"
  ]
}
